Subject: Serialize the C library's path and descriptor-table calls on ARM

What: run every path call (open, stat, lstat, opendir, readdir, closedir,
     mkdir, rmdir, unlink, rename, chmod, utimes, symlink, readlink,
     realpath, getcwd, chdir) and every descriptor-table call (close, dup,
     lseek, fstat, ftruncate, fchmod) under one process-wide mutex, and
     take errno inside it. Reads and writes are not gated.
Why: the native Pi system's posixc (2026-08-22) gives pthread workers no
     library base of their own. All threads share one base, its path
     conversion buffer (reallocated per call), descriptor table and errno.
     Four threads doing stat/read on their own files read each other's
     files and errno; VectorCraft's GUI failed to open files (EINVAL) and
     corrupted the TLSF heap. Same approach as libc-aros b060307 on x86_64.
Scope: AArch64 PAL imported from jonx/rust-aros 2e2845efb6aaa111b5a26c9685e96d08fad340f4.
License: MIT OR Apache-2.0, matching the original Jonx/Rust source files.
Upstream status: local integration patch; no submission authorized.

